# OpenBB Provider API Keys
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the keys you have.
# See README.md in this directory for provider details and signup links.
#
# Pattern: the provider's DECLARED CREDENTIAL NAME, upper-cased (no OPENBB_ prefix).
# That is usually {PROVIDER}_API_KEY but NOT always — tiingo declares `tiingo_token`
# and cftc declares `cftc_app_token`. Verified 2026-08-10 against the installed
# registry; check a new one before adding it:
#   python -c "from openbb_core.provider.registry import RegistryLoader as R; \
#              print(R.from_extensions().providers['tiingo'].credentials)"
#
# 32 providers are installed. These 17 need NO key at all:
#   cboe deribit ecb famafrench federal_reserve finra finviz government_us imf
#   multpl oecd sec seeking_alpha stockgrid tmx wsj yfinance

# === Free API keys (recommended) ===
# FMP_API_KEY=
# FRED_API_KEY=
# POLYGON_API_KEY=   # NOT INSTALLED — openbb[all] does not ship openbb-polygon.
#                    # Setting this does nothing until the package is added.
# ALPHA_VANTAGE_API_KEY=
# TIINGO_TOKEN=   # CORRECT as written — tiingo declares `tiingo_token`, not an api_key
# NASDAQ_API_KEY=
# BLS_API_KEY=
# CONGRESS_GOV_API_KEY=
# CFTC_APP_TOKEN=   # a Socrata app token, not an api_key
# ECONDB_API_KEY=
# BIZTOC_API_KEY=
# EIA_API_KEY=

# === Paid providers ===
# BENZINGA_API_KEY=
# INTRINIO_API_KEY=
# TRADIER_API_KEY=
# TRADIER_ACCOUNT_TYPE=sandbox
# TRADINGECONOMICS_API_KEY=
